Z||000008||BellaFiero||09-27-2000||12:24 PM||||All right, Haze, you can drive the submarine. Okay, here's the fall-back plan if the frontal assault doesn't work - we're all Olympic athletes. Haze, you say to the Evil Pontiac Guard : "Yes, we Olympians were just going to have a gander at these cars, see... ah, there's one of those nasty Fieros now... never could stand that car" ... and then My7Fieros can smack him silly with the baton... and then, my friends, it's smooth sailing. Just gas em up and drive em to the sub... unless of course the fuel filters are clogged from sitting for so long... then I guess Haze will just have to carry them all on his back....||||reg||10
Z||000009||Fformula88||09-27-2000||05:24 PM||||Ok, here is the story so far.<P>The cars ARE NOT in Australia, but rather in the Pontiac Special Vehicles Warehouse in Michigan.  The pictures were from an Australian tour that posts an internet Pontiac newsletter.  The pictures are claimed to have been taken in 1999.<P>I have no idea if these cars do actually exist.  I have also heard info third hand that supposedly originated from Hulki Aldikacti that all of the prototypes were destroyed.  <P>No one seems to know anymore about it, so I am trying to dig up more info from Pontiac about it.  Since a tour was allowed to snap pictures of them (if they do exist) then I wouldn't think Pontiac would mind confirming their existence.  I am hoping to hear back from them soon.  When and if I do, I will certainly post it!<P>In the meantime, keep the rescue plans coming and let me know what I can do!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
