Z||000014||Bald Dude||09-28-2000||06:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>Ok, here is the story so far.<P>The cars ARE NOT in Australia, but rather in the Pontiac Special Vehicles Warehouse in Michigan.  The pictures were from an Australian tour that posts an internet Pontiac newsletter.  The pictures are claimed to have been taken in 1999.<P>I have no idea if these cars do actually exist.  I have also heard info third hand that supposedly originated from Hulki Aldikacti that all of the prototypes were destroyed.  <P>No one seems to know anymore about it, so I am trying to dig up more info from Pontiac about it.  Since a tour was allowed to snap pictures of them (if they do exist) then I wouldn't think Pontiac would mind confirming their existence.  I am hoping to hear back from them soon.  When and if I do, I will certainly post it!<P>In the meantime, keep the rescue plans coming and let me know what I can do!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Woo-Hoo!!  Keep that info coming!  Also count me in on any rescue plans!<P>BTW,  When I wrote to Pontiac and ask them to revive the Fiero or something close they were very polite and told me that this or similar cars did not fit in with current marketing plans. . .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  I can't believe they would build an aztek but not a mid-engine sport coupe?  From the General's sports performance division?  Go Figure.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Mark<BR>||||reg||1
